(2229128, 304103, 37893, '<td valign="top">For every few folks that do like an image, there are some that don''t. Unfortunately it is something that we have to come to terms with. <br/> <br/>With that said, I think this fits perfect for the challenge. The vibrant colors stand out and the expression on Peter''s face is unmistakeable. Kinda like saying, "poor me. look at what my wife is doing". LOL!<br/> <br/>Anyway, it seems just a tad oversharpened as seen in the flower on his chest. I like the overall feel of this image. All except for the red border. Had it been thinner, maybe 1 pixel, it would be better IMHO. FWIW, this one got an 8 from me ;)</td>', 'For every few folks that do like an image, there are some that don''t. Unfortunately it is something that we have to come to terms with.  With that said, I think this fits perfect for the challenge. The vibrant colors stand out and the expression on Peter''s face is unmistakeable. Kinda like saying, "poor me. look at what my wife is doing". LOL! Anyway, it seems just a tad oversharpened as seen in the flower on his chest. I like the overall feel of this image. All except for the red border. Had it been thinner, maybe 1 pixel, it would be better IMHO. FWIW, this one got an 8 from me ;)', '2006-03-15 02:11:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2229141, 303998, 35078, '<td valign="top">Very clever! Well done.</td>', 'Very clever! Well done.', '2006-03-15 02:22:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2229151, 304039, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> I''ll come out and say publically, I gave this a 2<br/>Superb shot, but have a real hard time with this image standing on it''s own in this challenge without the title being crucial to the force fit.<br/>I do think out of the box by the way, but maybe my box is a bit small.<br/> <br/>I know, how to win friends here....nothing personal. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for commenting Brad. I know this was difficult to see - but I really tried to get the shot looking this way (with the "alien" looking at us earthlings). It''s not just a image I gave a name to. However, this is a learning curve for me and I will try to make my entries more "challenge fitting" in the future.<br/>Kind regards,<br/>Irene</td>', 'Originally posted by BradP: I''ll come out and say publically, I gave this a 2Superb shot, but have a real hard time with this image standing on it''s own in this challenge without the title being crucial to the force fit.I do think out of the box by the way, but maybe my box is a bit small. I know, how to win friends here....nothing personal.   Thanks for commenting Brad. I know this was difficult to see - but I really tried to get the shot looking this way (with the "alien" looking at us earthlings). It''s not just a image I gave a name to. However, this is a learning curve for me and I will try to make my entries more "challenge fitting" in the future.Kind regards,Irene', '2006-03-15 02:37:26.000000', NULL, 0),
