(2237086, 302571, 53863, '<td valign="top">I mainly got this idea from a time at a restaurant where a friend ordered a drink and I seriously thought it looked just like antifreeze.  I''m going to have to find that drink and compare it to the antifreeze.  Thanks for all the comments!  When I was working on the levels I was debating on how to set the brightness.  Since my monitor is calibrated and I work in a dimly lit room I suppose that the detail I see is easily washed out on a monitor that isn''t calibrated.  Oh well, I suppose that is something to consider in future challenges.  I only had a flashlight to work with for the lighting so I figure this turned out pretty well considering.  Good for my first post....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-18 03:56:33.</i></td>', 'I mainly got this idea from a time at a restaurant where a friend ordered a drink and I seriously thought it looked just like antifreeze.  I''m going to have to find that drink and compare it to the antifreeze.  Thanks for all the comments!  When I was working on the levels I was debating on how to set the brightness.  Since my monitor is calibrated and I work in a dimly lit room I suppose that the detail I see is easily washed out on a monitor that isn''t calibrated.  Oh well, I suppose that is something to consider in future challenges.  I only had a flashlight to work with for the lighting so I figure this turned out pretty well considering.  Good for my first post....', '2006-03-18 03:50:01.000000', '2006-03-18 03:56:33.000000', 0),
